        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid winning cards and tricks that score penalty points. Six hands played in sequence with different objectives. Lowest total score after six hands wins.',
          gameplay: 'Six hands played in fixed order: 1. No tricks - each trick = 10 pts (130 total). 2. No hearts - each heart = 10 pts (130 total). 3. No queens - each queen = 25 pts (100 total). 4. No king of spades - Kâ™  = 100 pts. 5. No last trick - last trick = 100 pts. 6. Combination - all above penalties apply (560 total). Player left of dealer leads. Must follow suit if possible; if cannot, may play any card. Highest card of led suit wins trick. No trumps. Winner leads to next trick.',
          keyRules: [
            '3-6 players, 52-card deck (adjusted for player count)',
            '6 hands played in fixed sequence',
            'Hand 1: No tricks (10 pts each)',
            'Hand 2: No hearts (10 pts each)',
            'Hand 3: No queens (25 pts each)',
            'Hand 4: No king of spades (100 pts)',
            'Hand 5: No last trick (100 pts)',
            'Hand 6: All penalties combined',
            'Must follow suit, no trumps',
            'Lowest total score wins',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Try to avoid winning tricks, especially in hands 1, 5, and 6. Get rid of high cards in dangerous suits early. In hand 4, avoid the king of spades at all costs.',
          intermediate: 'Count cards to track dangerous cards. In hand 2 (no hearts), try to become void in hearts early so you can discard them when other suits are led. In hand 6, the penalties stack dramatically - a single trick can cost hundreds of points.',
          advanced: 'Duck tricks by playing middle cards when possible. Force opponents to win dangerous tricks. In hand 6, calculate the maximum penalty a trick could cost. Long-term strategy across all six hands - sometimes taking a small penalty early prevents a larger one later.',
          tips: [
            'In Hand 2 (no hearts), try to get void in hearts early',
            'Save low cards for when you must win a trick',
            'In Hand 4, the Kâ™  is the only card that matters - everything else is safe',
            'Hand 6 is brutal - a single trick can cost 175+ points',
            'Track which queens have been played in Hand 3',
            'In Hand 5, everyone tries to avoid the last trick',
            'Sometimes you must win a trick to avoid winning a worse one later',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
